check.model:
(1) OID → {ODATE, CID}; CID → {CNAME, CPHONE}; PID → {PNAME, UNITPRICE}; {OID, PID} → QTY.
Not 2NF: ODATE, CID depend only on OID and PNAME, UNITPRICE only on PID (partial dependencies on part of the composite key).
Not 3NF: after splitting, ORDERS(OID, ODATE, CID, CNAME, CPHONE) has OID → CID → {CNAME, CPHONE}, a transitive dependency.

(2)
CREATE TABLE CUSTOMER (CID INT PRIMARY KEY, CNAME VARCHAR(30), CPHONE CHAR(8));
CREATE TABLE PRODUCT (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30), UNITPRICE DECIMAL(8,2));
CREATE TABLE ORDERS (OID INT PRIMARY KEY, ODATE DATE, CID INT NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (CID) REFERENCES CUSTOMER(CID));
CREATE TABLE ORDERITEM (OID INT, PID INT, QTY INT, PRIMARY KEY (OID, PID),
  FOREIGN KEY (OID) REFERENCES ORDERS(OID),
  FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PRODUCT(PID));

pr.solution:
CREATE TABLE CUSTOMER (CID INT PRIMARY KEY, CNAME VARCHAR(30), CPHONE CHAR(8));
CREATE TABLE PRODUCT (PID INT PRIMARY KEY, PNAME VARCHAR(30), UNITPRICE DECIMAL(8,2));
CREATE TABLE ORDERS (OID INT PRIMARY KEY, ODATE DATE, CID INT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY (CID) REFERENCES CUSTOMER(CID));
CREATE TABLE ORDERITEM (OID INT, PID INT, QTY INT, PRIMARY KEY (OID, PID), FOREIGN KEY (OID) REFERENCES ORDERS(OID), FOREIGN KEY (PID) REFERENCES PRODUCT(PID));
